===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ostler}}

===Etymology===
Syncopated form of {{m|en|hosteler}}, from {{inh|en|enm|hostiler}}, from {{der|en|frm|hostiler}}, from {{der|en|fro|hostelier}}, from {{der|en|ML.|hostilārius}}, {{m|la|hospitālārius}}, from {{m|la|hospitāle}} "inn", from {{m|la|hospitālis}} "hospitable", from {{m|la|hospes}} "host, guest". Both hostler and its alternate form {{m|en|ostler}} originally meant simply "innkeeper", and acquired a specific association with horses in the second half of the 14th century. Doublet of {{m|en|hotelier}}.

